most commonly used Retriever types in LangChain.

| Retriever Type                       | Purpose                                                                                                   | Best Use Case                                                | Real-Time Example                                                                                                             |
| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **VectorStoreRetriever**             | Retrieves documents using vector similarity search from vector databases like FAISS, Chroma, or Pinecone. | Standard RAG applications.                                   | A bus booking chatbot retrieves bus policies from a FAISS index.                                                              |
| **ContextualCompressionRetriever**   | Retrieves relevant documents and compresses them, keeping only the most useful parts.                     | Very large documents where only a few paragraphs are needed. | A PDF of 300 pages is reduced to only the paragraphs about cancellation policies.                                             |
| **MultiQueryRetriever**              | Generates multiple search queries from one user question to improve recall.                               | Ambiguous or broad questions.                                | User asks "Tell me about AI agents." The retriever searches for "Agentic AI", "Autonomous Agents", and "Multi-Agent Systems". |
| **ParentDocumentRetriever**          | Retrieves a small matching chunk and then returns the larger parent document for context.                 | When a complete section or article is needed.                | A sentence matches in a user manual, but the chatbot returns the full chapter containing that sentence.                       |
| **BM25Retriever**                    | Uses traditional keyword-based retrieval (BM25 algorithm) instead of embeddings.                          | Exact keyword matching.                                      | Searching legal documents or product codes where exact words matter.                                                          |
| **EnsembleRetriever**                | Combines results from multiple retrievers (for example, VectorStore + BM25).                              | Hybrid search systems.                                       | A restaurant chatbot combines semantic search with keyword search for better menu retrieval.                                  |
| **TimeWeightedVectorStoreRetriever** | Combines semantic similarity with document recency. Newer documents receive higher priority.              | News, chat history, or frequently updated data.              | An AI news chatbot prefers today's articles over articles from last month.                                                    |
| **TavilySearchAPIRetriever**         | Uses Tavily to retrieve live information from the web.                                                    | Current events, breaking news, and internet search.          | "Latest AI news today" or "Current weather in Chennai."                                                                       |
